.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-schema-rm - Remove a type or a field from the local repository


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work schema rm KEY | --id ID [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a type's or a field's local ref. This is local: the entity comes back on
the next pull. The replicated removal is archive.

.PP
KEY is a type key or a field key, /\&. A KEY two entities hold is
refused, naming both ids: name one with --id ID, a full id or a unique prefix,
archived or not, which is never read as a key.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rm

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	name the entity by its id or a unique prefix of it, archived or not, instead of by KEY


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
git work schema rm task/estimate
git work schema rm --id db9cdb7
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-schema(1)\fP
